{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3f928b818a5978b37bb74f0a1124b6d0249a6c2d6819ac666f2a19464034f6a5","digest":{"component_or_area":"usage logging / LLM runner","key_entities":["PydanticAIRunner.run()","usage_log.record()","usage_log.record_failure()","interpret_failure()","REBAR_USAGE_LOG","src/rebar/llm/runner.py","src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py","step_identity","OUTCOME_OK","OUTCOME_FAILED","failure_usage()","run_messages"],"problem_keywords":["usage log","failed calls","llm error handling","missing records","spend tracking","telemetry"],"propositions":["when PydanticAIRunner.run() raises an exception, usage_log.record() is never called because it sits after the except block, leaving no usage row for failed calls","failed LLM calls burn tokens and incur costs that are invisible in the usage log JSONL, causing spend totals and per-step attribution to silently underreport actual usage","per-step attribution added by change b690 cannot identify which steps failed or how much budget they consumed, only successful steps are visible","the fix must record failed calls with an explicit outcome marker to distinguish burned budget from delivered work, and must not convert or swallow the provider exception"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787369285256783001,"uuid":"e0f7367a-787e-4674-a50a-709006f41b0a"}